{
  "doc": [
    "The exchanges of RFC 0001's mcpworkspace wire, in order, each a JSON-RPC request sent with the next id after an MCP initialization, and its result or error.",
    "The served workspace: inside.txt (ok), sub/a.txt (a), alias.txt -> inside.txt, linkout -> ../outside/secret.txt; a file k/<kind>, and a start of kind:<kind>, refused with that kind (other: with none), its served text naming /srv/hidden/<kind>; two servers offered, echo and holder (given a secret), both cat.",
    "A params' \"${port}\" is a port on the loopback that answers what it is sent, upper-cased, once all of it is sent.",
    "A read asks for less than all the process wrote, so that whether it reaches the end does not depend on timing.",
    "A resource's text is JSON, shown with its keys sorted; ${root} stands for the served root, and * for what differs between runs.",
    "mcpworkspace/corpus_test.go replays it against the reference server, and maps its refusals back through the reference client."
  ],
  "exchanges": [
    {
      "name": "what the server keeps",
      "method": "agentworkspace/process.info",
      "params": {},
      "result": {
        "bounds": {
          "maxProcesses": 32,
          "maxReadBytes": 65536,
          "maxWriteBytes": 1048576
        },
        "reach": "*"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "list the servers offered: holder is marked as given a secret, and nothing of it is told",
      "method": "agentworkspace/servers.list",
      "params": {},
      "result": {
        "servers": [
          {
            "description": "says it back",
            "name": "echo"
          },
          {
            "description": "holds a token",
            "name": "holder",
            "secrets": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
